   "text": {
    "L1": "A line of symmetry folds a shape into two mirror images.",
    "L2": "The halves must lie exactly on top of each other. Equal-sized halves alone are not enough.",
    "L3": "A square has four lines of symmetry, while a rectangle that is not a square has two.",
    "L4": "A circle has endless lines of symmetry because every line through its centre works.",
    "L5": "Let us test a rectangle by folding it top to bottom and side to side.",
    "L6": "Both folds match exactly, so these are the rectangle's two lines of symmetry.",
    "L7": "A corner-to-corner fold makes equal-sized triangles, but the corners do not match.",
    "L8": "So check by folding or using a mirror, then count only exact matches."
   },
